124500**************************************************
124600*                                                *
124700*   THIS ROUTINE LOCKS THE MREQFILE DATA SET SO  *
124800*   THAT NO MORE PROCESSING CAN BE DONE TO IT    *
124900*   AND THEN READS EVERY ENTRY AND WRITES THEM   *
125000*   TO REQ-FILE2 AND THEN DELETES THEM FROM THE  *
125100*   MREQFILE DATA SET.  THIS IS DONE TO INSURE   *
125200*   THAT ALL ENTRIES ARE PROCESSED ONLY ONCE     *
125300*   YET NOT TIE UP THE MREQFILE DATA SET THE     *
125400*   ENTIRE TIME THIS PROGRAM IS RUNNING.         *
125500*                                                *
125600**************************************************
125700
125800 60-READ-MREQFILE.
           READ MREQFILE-O NEXT INTO BUF-MREQFILE
               AT END MOVE FILE-STATUS TO FILE-STATUS.
           IF FILE-STATUS NOT = "00"
               IF FILE-STATUS = "10" OR "14"
128100             GO TO 60-CLOSE-REQFILE2
128200         ELSE
128300             MOVE "GET MREQFILE * 60-GM" TO BU-DISPLAY-MSG
128400             GO TO 2-BLOWUP.
128500
      *    ACCEPT IOFEEDBACK FROM I-O-FEEDBACK-AREA.
      *    DISPLAY "IO-REL-NO=", IO-REL-NO.
128600
128700     MOVE MREQFILE-CORP-CODE-7     TO  REQ-CORP-CODE.
128800     MOVE MREQFILE-REQ-STATUS      TO  REQ-RETURN-SW.
128900     MOVE MREQFILE-REQ-NUM-MMIS    TO  REQ-NUM-MMIS.
129000     WRITE REQ-RCD.

           DELETE MREQFILE-O
               INVALID KEY MOVE FILE-STATUS TO FILE-STATUS.
           IF FILE-STATUS NOT = "00"
131600         MOVE "DELETE MREQFILE * 60-RM" TO BU-DISPLAY-MSG
131700         GO TO 2-BLOWUP.
133100
129100     GO TO 60-READ-MREQFILE.
129200
129300 60-CLOSE-REQFILE2.
129400     CLOSE REQ-FILE2.

133200 60-RM-X.
133300     EXIT.
