133500*********************************************
133600*                                           *
133700*  THIS PROCEDURES READS ALL CODES IN       *
133800*  'REQ-FILE2' . IF THE CODE IS A           *
133900*  RAW MATERIAL IT IS STORED IN A TEMP FILE *
134000*  (RAWMAT-TEMP). THE PURPOSE IS TO ASSURE  *
134100*  ALL RAW MATERIALS ARE WITHIN A REQ. NO.  *
134200*  SEQ.  IF CODE IS NOT A RAW MATERIAL      *
134300*  THEN PROCESS A REQ.  IF RETURN-SW IS     *
134400*  EQUAL TO "R" WRITE CODE TO A TEMP FILE   *
134500*  (REORDER-TEMP) SO THESE CODES CAN GO ON  *
134600*  REORDER REPORT. IF IT IS A "E" WRITE     *
134700*  CODE TO A TEMP FILE (EXPEDITE-TEMP) SO   *
134800*  THESE CODES CAN GO ON A EXPEDITE REPORT  *
134900*  IF REQ-RETURN-SW IS BLANK THEN CREATE A  *
135000*  REQUISTION. IF THE REQ-RETURN-SW IS AN   *
135100*  'A' THEN CHECK IT FOR SUFFICIENT ONORDER *
135200*  AND OPEN REQS. IF IT DOES NOT MEET ANY   *
135300*  OF THIS CRITEREA THEN CREATE A REQ.      *
135400*                                           *
135500*********************************************
135600 60-READ-REQ-FILE.
135700     READ REQ-FILE2 AT END
135800         GO TO 60-RRF-X.
135900
136000     IF REQ-CODE-1-2  =  "26" OR "27"
136100         MOVE REQ-CORP-CODE    TO RAWMAT-CODE
136200         MOVE REQ-RETURN-SW    TO RAWMAT-SW
136300         MOVE REQ-NUM-MMIS     TO RAWMAT-NUM-MMIS
136400         WRITE RAWMAT-RCD
136500         GO TO 60-READ-REQ-FILE.
136700

136800     IF REQ-RETURN-SW  =  "R"
136900         PERFORM 63-RETURN-REQ  THRU  63-R-R-X
137000     ELSE
137100     IF REQ-RETURN-SW  =  "E"
137200         PERFORM 64-EXPEDITE-REQ  THRU  64-E-R-X
137300     ELSE
137400     IF REQ-RETURN-SW  =  "A"
